---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { approvedCopy, contactEmail, siteName } from "../content/site";
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy and contact information">
  <section id="privacy-scope" class="page-section reading" data-section="U1">
    <h1 class="utility-title">Privacy and contact information</h1>

    <p>
      This website explains {siteName}, provides an AI-assisted Parkinson's
      research exploration tool, and invites project inquiries. The website
      does not offer user accounts or intentionally collect medical records.
    </p>

    <p>
      Please do not submit medical records, names, addresses, account numbers,
      or other sensitive personal or health information through the AI research
      tool or project email.
    </p>

    <p><a href="/#introduction">Back to the introduction</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-responsibility" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>

    <p>{approvedCopy.responsibleOperator}</p>
    <p>Contact: <span class="email-address">{contactEmail}</span></p>

    <p>
      This notice applies to the public Meridian Station website, the
      AI-assisted research question feature, and the project's dedicated email
      channel.
    </p>

    <p>
      Meridian Station is not operating a clinical service, patient portal, or
      medical-record system through this website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-ai" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>AI-assisted research questions</h2>

    <p>
      When you submit a question through Ask Parkinson's Insights, the text of
      your question is sent to Meridian Station's server-side service for
      processing. The request is handled by a Firebase Cloud Function operated
      on Google infrastructure and is then sent to the OpenAI API so an answer
      can be generated.
    </p>

    <p>
      Meridian Station does not intentionally save your question or the
      generated answer in a project database, browser storage, or conversation
      history. The current tool processes one question at a time.
    </p>

    <p>
      The service providers involved in processing the request may maintain
      operational, security, abuse-prevention, or service logs according to
      their own service practices. Provider-controlled records are not fully
      controlled by Meridian Station.
    </p>

    <p>
      OpenAI states that information submitted through its API is not used to
      train or improve its models by default. OpenAI may retain API content and
      related metadata for abuse monitoring and service operation according to
      its applicable API data-retention practices.
    </p>

    <p>
      Because the research tool is intended for general educational and
      research questions, do not submit medical records or other sensitive
      identifying information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-email" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>If you email</h2>

    <p>
      Your email includes your address, the message you choose to send, and
      information handled by the email services involved. Please send only a
      short project-related inquiry and avoid medical records or other
      sensitive material.
    </p>

    <p>{approvedCopy.authorizedRecipient}</p>
    <p>{approvedCopy.correspondencePurposes}</p>

    <p>
      Contacting the project does not enroll you in a study or subscribe you to
      marketing. We will ask separately before publicly quoting or crediting a
      message.
    </p>

    <h3>Email handling and retention</h3>
    <p>{approvedCopy.emailPolicy}</p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-visiting" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>Visiting the website</h2>

    <p>
      Meridian Station does not currently use advertising trackers, analytics,
      application cookies, browser storage, or a service worker on the public
      site.
    </p>

    <p>
      The website is delivered through Firebase Hosting. Firebase Hosting may
      process technical request information, including IP addresses, to provide
      the service, detect abuse, and support infrastructure operations.
    </p>

    <h3>Server-side processing and logs</h3>

    <p>
      Requests to the AI research feature are processed by a Firebase Cloud
      Function deployed in the United States. Cloud Functions automatically
      generates operational logs in Google Cloud Logging. Meridian Station's
      application code is designed not to intentionally log the submitted
      question, generated answer, OpenAI API key, or other sensitive request
      content.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google may process Firebase service data on infrastructure operated by
      Google or its service providers according to the applicable Firebase and
      Google Cloud terms. Some Firebase services operate on global
      infrastructure even when a specific function executes in a selected
      region.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-third-parties" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>Service providers</h2>

    <p>
      Meridian Station currently uses Firebase and Google Cloud infrastructure
      for website delivery and server-side processing, OpenAI for generation of
      AI-assisted research answers, and Cloudflare Email Routing for forwarding
      project email.
    </p>

    <p>
      These providers may process technical, request, or message-routing
      information as necessary to provide their services. Meridian Station does
      not control every infrastructure location, operational log, backup, or
      provider security record maintained by these services.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-requests" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>Questions, deletion, or an accidental disclosure</h2>

    <p>
      If you have a question about information handling or want to request
      deletion of project correspondence, use
      <a href="/#collaborate">Contact about privacy</a>. Please identify the
      relevant correspondence without resending health records or other
      sensitive material.
    </p>

    <p>
      This link returns to the collaboration and contact section; it does not
      itself submit a request.
    </p>

    <p>{approvedCopy.requestPolicy}</p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-dates" class="page-section reading">
    <h2>Notice dates</h2>

    <p>Effective: October 31, 2026</p>
    <p>Last reviewed: October 31, 2026</p>

    <ul class="utility-links">
      <li><a href="/#collaborate">Return to collaboration and contact</a></li>
      <li><a href="/#introduction">Back to the introduction</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>